# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Definisikan Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function takes the model as a dictionary with three keys. Each one accepts either a single float, which applies uniformly along the chain, or a list that specifies the value site by site. Lists have $L-1$ entries for `hopping_amplitude`, because an open chain has one fewer bond than sites, and $L$ entries for `on_site_interaction` and `chemical_potential`.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini menerima model sebagai dictionary dengan tiga key. Masing-masing menerima satu float tunggal, yang berlaku seragam di sepanjang rantai, atau sebuah list yang menentukan nilai per situs. List berisi $L-1$ entri untuk `hopping_amplitude`, karena rantai terbuka punya satu ikatan lebih sedikit daripada jumlah situs, dan $L$ entri untuk `on_site_interaction` dan `chemical_potential`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses a uniform chain of 31 sites with a repulsive interaction $U/t_h = 8$. A uniform chemical potential contributes only a global phase when the particle number is fixed, so this example sets it to zero. The chemical potential matters only when it varies from site to site, for example, to add disorder or a single impurity.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai rantai seragam dengan 31 situs dan interaksi tolak-menolak $U/t_h = 8$. Potensial kimia yang seragam hanya menyumbang fase global ketika jumlah partikel tetap, jadi contoh ini menetapkannya ke nol. Potensial kimia baru berpengaruh ketika nilainya berbeda dari situs ke situs, misalnya untuk menambahkan disorder atau satu pengotor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the Trotter schedule {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"
msgstr "Atur jadwal Trotter {#set-the-trotter-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `simulation` dictionary holds the time step ($\\Delta t$) and the number of Trotter steps, and the total evolution time is their product. Larger steps reach later times at fixed circuit depth but incur more Trotter error, which grows with $U$ because the Hamiltonian terms commute less. The published hardware study used $\\Delta t = 0.15$ for $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), and this tutorial uses the same value. Circuit depth grows linearly in the step count and does not depend on $L$ at all.\n"
msgstr "Dictionary `simulation` berisi langkah waktu ($\\Delta t$) dan jumlah langkah Trotter, dan total waktu evolusi adalah hasil kali keduanya. Langkah yang lebih besar mencapai waktu yang lebih lama pada kedalaman circuit tetap, tetapi menimbulkan lebih banyak error Trotter, yang tumbuh seiring $U$ karena suku-suku Hamiltonian makin kurang komut. Studi hardware yang dipublikasikan memakai $\\Delta t = 0.15$ untuk $U/t_h = 8$ [\\[2\\]](#references), dan tutorial ini memakai nilai yang sama. Kedalaman circuit tumbuh secara linear terhadap jumlah langkah dan sama sekali tidak bergantung pada $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the initial state {#prepare-the-initial-state}"
msgstr "Siapkan keadaan awal {#prepare-the-initial-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each site holds two spin orbitals, so an $L$-site chain uses $2L$ qubits. The initial state is a Fock occupation string with one character per site:\n"
msgstr "Setiap situs menampung dua orbital spin, jadi rantai dengan $L$ situs memakai $2L$ qubit. Keadaan awalnya adalah string okupansi Fock dengan satu karakter per situs:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\texttt{empty (e)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{up (u)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,0), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{down (d)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (0,1), \\\\\n"
"\\texttt{both (b)} &\\longleftrightarrow \\left(n_{i,\\uparrow}, n_{i,\\downarrow}\\right) = (1,1).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The string is read least significant site first, so the rightmost character is site 0 and the physical site index of character $k$ counted from the left is $i = L - 1 - k$. The string `udud` therefore means site 0 is `d`, site 1 is `u`, site 2 is `d`, and site 3 is `u`.\n"
msgstr "String dibaca dengan situs paling tidak signifikan lebih dulu, jadi karakter paling kanan adalah situs 0 dan indeks situs fisik dari karakter $k$ yang dihitung dari kiri adalah $i = L - 1 - k$. Jadi string `udud` berarti situs 0 adalah `d`, situs 1 adalah `u`, situs 2 adalah `d`, dan situs 3 adalah `u`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, prepare a half-filled Néel state, alternating `u` and `d`, with the central site replaced by a vacancy. The vacancy is the disturbance whose spreading is tracked.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, siapkan keadaan Néel half-filled, dengan `u` dan `d` bergantian, dan situs tengah diganti dengan kekosongan (vacancy). Kekosongan ini adalah gangguan yang penyebarannya dilacak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the observables {#build-the-observables}"
msgstr "Bangun observabel {#build-the-observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each observable is a dictionary that represents a weighted sum of products of occupation operators:\n"
msgstr "Setiap observabel adalah dictionary yang merepresentasikan jumlah berbobot dari hasil kali operator okupansi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"O = \\sum_{\\alpha} c_{\\alpha} \\prod_{(\\sigma, j) \\in T_{\\alpha}} n_{j,\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every entry of `operators` is one term $T_{\\alpha}$, written as a list of `[name, site]` pairs that multiply together, and the matching entry of `coefficients` is its weight. The two names are `\"Nup\"` for $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ and `\"Ndn\"` for $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. A single one-point observable $n_{3,\\uparrow}$ is written as follows:\n"
msgstr "Setiap entri `operators` adalah satu suku $T_{\\alpha}$, ditulis sebagai list pasangan `[name, site]` yang dikalikan, dan entri `coefficients` yang bersesuaian adalah bobotnya. Dua nama yang dipakai adalah `\"Nup\"` untuk $n_{j,\\uparrow}$ dan `\"Ndn\"` untuk $n_{j,\\downarrow}$. Satu observabel satu-titik $n_{3,\\uparrow}$ ditulis sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell prints the smallest complete set of inputs the function accepts, which is useful as a shape reference while reading the code that follows.\n"
msgstr "Sel berikutnya mencetak himpunan input lengkap terkecil yang diterima fungsi, yang berguna sebagai acuan bentuk saat membaca kode selanjutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three groups of observables are needed. The charge density $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ and the local spin $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ are both two-term sums over the same operators, differing only in their coefficients. The spin correlator $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ between site $i$ and the vacancy site expands into four two-point terms with coefficients $\\pm 1/4$.\n"
msgstr "Dibutuhkan tiga kelompok observabel. Kerapatan muatan $n_i = n_{i\\uparrow} + n_{i\\downarrow}$ dan spin lokal $S^z_i = (n_{i\\uparrow} - n_{i\\downarrow})/2$ keduanya adalah jumlah dua suku dari operator yang sama, hanya berbeda pada koefisiennya. Korelator spin $S^z_i S^z_{i_*}$ antara situs $i$ dan situs kekosongan diuraikan menjadi empat suku dua-titik dengan koefisien $\\pm 1/4$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Occupation operators commute, so the order of factors within a term is irrelevant, but the order of the `observables` list fixes the order of the returned values. The code records an index for each group while it builds the list. The correlator skips the vacancy site, where the product would repeat a factor.\n"
msgstr "Operator okupansi saling komut, jadi urutan faktor dalam satu suku tidak berpengaruh, tetapi urutan list `observables` menentukan urutan nilai yang dikembalikan. Kode mencatat sebuah indeks untuk tiap kelompok saat membangun list. Korelator melewati situs kekosongan, karena di sana hasil kali akan mengulang satu faktor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi di hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial has no transpilation step. The function performs the following steps internally [\\[2\\]](#references), and you cannot configure them from the notebook:\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini tidak punya langkah transpilasi. Fungsi ini melakukan langkah-langkah berikut secara internal [\\[2\\]](#references), dan kamu tidak bisa mengonfigurasinya dari notebook:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps the fermionic modes to qubits under an ordering chosen to keep Pauli weights low on a heavy-hex lattice\n"
msgstr "Memetakan mode fermionik ke qubit dengan urutan yang dipilih agar bobot Pauli tetap rendah pada kisi heavy-hex\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uses a fermionic SWAP network so every hopping term becomes a two-qubit rotation\n"
msgstr "Memakai jaringan SWAP fermionik sehingga setiap suku hopping menjadi rotasi dua-qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embeds the chain along a path that avoids weak qubits\n"
msgstr "Menanamkan rantai di sepanjang jalur yang menghindari qubit lemah\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applies dynamical decoupling and Pauli twirling during compilation\n"
msgstr "Menerapkan dynamical decoupling dan Pauli twirling selama kompilasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You choose the backend and the shot count. The function takes a backend name as a string, so this tutorial selects the least busy device large enough for the chain and passes its name.\n"
msgstr "Kamu memilih backend dan jumlah shot. Fungsi ini menerima nama backend sebagai string, jadi tutorial ini memilih perangkat paling sepi antrean yang cukup besar untuk rantai tersebut dan mengirimkan namanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The smallest signal that you need to resolve sets the shot count. The charge tracer reaches amplitudes near $0.15$, but the connected spin tracer peaks around $0.04$, roughly four times smaller. The published study used 20,000 shots per circuit for this reason [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Sinyal terkecil yang perlu kamu resolusikan menentukan jumlah shot. Tracer muatan mencapai amplitudo sekitar $0.15$, tetapi tracer spin terhubung memuncak sekitar $0.04$, kira-kira empat kali lebih kecil. Studi yang dipublikasikan memakai 20.000 shot per circuit karena alasan ini [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute by using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi dengan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-by-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, submit the simulation. `run` returns a job handle immediately rather than blocking.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, kirim simulasinya. `run` langsung mengembalikan job handle tanpa menunggu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `job.status()` to follow progress and `job.result()` to block until the job finishes. The result is a mapping whose `observable_expectation_values` entry is indexed first by observable, in the order they were supplied, and then by time. There are `step_count + 1` time points because the value at $t=0$ is included.\n"
msgstr "Pakai `job.status()` untuk mengikuti progres dan `job.result()` untuk menunggu sampai job selesai. Hasilnya adalah mapping yang entri `observable_expectation_values`-nya diindeks pertama menurut observabel, sesuai urutan saat diberikan, lalu menurut waktu. Ada `step_count + 1` titik waktu karena nilai pada $t=0$ ikut disertakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reconstruct the correlators {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"
msgstr "Rekonstruksi korelator {#reconstruct-the-correlators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split the flat array back into the three groups using the indices recorded earlier, then form the two tracer correlators. The charge tracer is the change in per-site density relative to $t=0$:\n"
msgstr "Pisahkan array datar kembali menjadi tiga kelompok memakai indeks yang dicatat sebelumnya, lalu bentuk dua korelator tracer. Tracer muatan adalah perubahan kerapatan per situs relatif terhadap $t=0$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^c_i(t) = \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(t) + n_{i\\downarrow}(t) \\rangle - \\langle n_{i\\uparrow}(0) + n_{i\\downarrow}(0) \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The spin tracer is the connected correlator between each site and the vacancy site $i_*$:\n"
msgstr "Tracer spin adalah korelator terhubung antara tiap situs dan situs kekosongan $i_*$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C^s_i(t) = 4 \\left( \\langle S^z_i S^z_{i_*} \\rangle - \\langle S^z_i \\rangle \\langle S^z_{i_*} \\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are built from Fock-basis operators, so they come from the same measured bitstrings and the second one costs no extra hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya dibangun dari operator basis Fock, jadi berasal dari bitstring terukur yang sama dan yang kedua tidak memakan eksekusi hardware tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you constructed the observables, the code recorded the position of each charge (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), and spin-correlation (`correlator_indices`) operator in the list. Because the simulator returns the expectation values in the same order, you can use these positions to extract the corresponding results. For the spin correlations, the code also uses `correlator_sites` to place each result at the correct lattice position, and leaves the vacancy as `NaN`.\n"
msgstr "Saat kamu membangun observabel, kode mencatat posisi tiap operator muatan (`charge_indices`), spin (`spin_indices`), dan korelasi spin (`correlator_indices`) di dalam list. Karena simulator mengembalikan nilai ekspektasi dengan urutan yang sama, kamu bisa memakai posisi ini untuk mengambil hasil yang sesuai. Untuk korelasi spin, kode juga memakai `correlator_sites` untuk menempatkan tiap hasil pada posisi kisi yang benar, dan membiarkan kekosongan sebagai `NaN`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the wavefronts {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"
msgstr "Visualisasikan front gelombang {#visualize-the-wavefronts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you plot each correlator as a heatmap of space and time, the light cone is directly visible. Time flows downward, and the horizontal axis is the position along the chain.\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu memplot tiap korelator sebagai heatmap ruang dan waktu, light cone langsung terlihat. Waktu mengalir ke bawah, dan sumbu horizontal adalah posisi di sepanjang rantai.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c75549b7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extract the wavefront velocities {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"
msgstr "Ekstrak kecepatan front gelombang {#extract-the-wavefront-velocities}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turn the heatmaps into numbers by following the detection protocol from the published study [\\[2\\]](#references). At each time slice, symmetrize the spatial profile about the vacancy, which averages away the antisymmetric part of the hardware noise, normalize by the largest off-center amplitude, and record the outermost site above a threshold. Detections are then cut into runs of consecutive time steps, and only the longest run is fit, which keeps the early-time transient out of the result.\n"
msgstr "Ubah heatmap menjadi angka dengan mengikuti protokol deteksi dari studi yang dipublikasikan [\\[2\\]](#references). Pada tiap irisan waktu, simetrikan profil spasial terhadap kekosongan, yang merata-ratakan bagian antisimetris dari noise hardware, normalisasi dengan amplitudo terbesar di luar pusat, dan catat situs terluar yang berada di atas ambang. Deteksi lalu dipotong menjadi run dari langkah waktu berurutan, dan hanya run terpanjang yang di-fit, sehingga transien waktu awal tidak ikut memengaruhi hasil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fitted velocity depends on the detection threshold and the trimming quantile, and that sensitivity dominates the shot noise. Scan both and report the median with the full envelope, as the published analysis does.\n"
msgstr "Kecepatan hasil fit bergantung pada ambang deteksi dan kuantil pemangkasan, dan sensitivitas itu mendominasi shot noise. Pindai keduanya dan laporkan median beserta envelope penuhnya, seperti yang dilakukan analisis yang dipublikasikan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/640db359-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drawing the detections back onto the heatmaps shows whether the algorithm tracked\n"
"the leading edge. Filled markers are the detections that entered\n"
"the fit. Open markers were cut by the masking rules, either because they sit too\n"
"close to the vacancy, too close to the chain end, or were late enough that the front has\n"
"broadened and its position is no longer sharp. The dashed line is the fit over the\n"
"times it used, and its slope is the velocity in each panel title.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggambar balik deteksi ke heatmap menunjukkan apakah algoritma melacak\n"
"tepi terdepan. Penanda terisi adalah deteksi yang masuk ke\n"
"fit. Penanda kosong dibuang oleh aturan masking, entah karena posisinya terlalu\n"
"dekat dengan kekosongan, terlalu dekat dengan ujung rantai, atau cukup terlambat sehingga front sudah\n"
"melebar dan posisinya tidak lagi tajam. Garis putus-putus adalah fit pada\n"
"waktu yang dipakainya, dan kemiringannya adalah kecepatan pada judul tiap panel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vacancy column is marked below the axis. The charge clips there because its value\n"
"is of order one, and spin has no value there, so it is drawn in gray.\n"
msgstr "Kolom vakansi ditandai di bawah sumbu. Muatan terpotong di sana karena nilainya berorde satu, sedangkan spin tidak punya nilai di sana, jadi digambar dengan warna abu-abu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The charge cone opens wider than the spin cone. Both disturbances leave the same\n"
"defect at the same moment and travel outward at different speeds.\n"
msgstr "Kerucut muatan terbuka lebih lebar daripada kerucut spin. Kedua gangguan meninggalkan cacat yang sama pada saat yang sama dan merambat keluar dengan kecepatan berbeda.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/fermi-hubbard-spin-charge-dynamics/extracted-outputs/25192e92-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The charge front outruns the spin front. A hole in a one-dimensional Mott background does not travel as an electron. Instead, it fractionalizes into a holon carrying the charge and a spinon carrying the spin disturbance, and at $U/t_h = 8$ the spinon is the slower of the two.\n"
msgstr "Front muatan mendahului front spin. Sebuah hole dalam latar Mott satu dimensi tidak merambat sebagai elektron. Sebaliknya, ia terpecah menjadi holon yang membawa muatan dan spinon yang membawa gangguan spin, dan pada $U/t_h = 8$ spinon adalah yang lebih lambat dari keduanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordering depends on the interaction. At $U = 0$, the model is free fermions with $v_c = 2$ and $v_s = 4$, so spin is faster. Repulsion suppresses spin transport while leaving charge transport nearly untouched, and by $U/t_h = 8$ the published hardware values are $v_c = 1.78$ and $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Rerunning with several values of $U$ and plotting $v_s / v_c$ maps the crossover.\n"
msgstr "Urutannya bergantung pada interaksi. Pada $U = 0$, modelnya adalah fermion bebas dengan $v_c = 2$ dan $v_s = 4$, jadi spin lebih cepat. Tolakan menekan transpor spin sementara transpor muatan nyaris tidak terpengaruh, dan pada $U/t_h = 8$ nilai perangkat keras yang dipublikasikan adalah $v_c = 1.78$ dan $v_s = 1.46$ [\\[2\\]](#references). Menjalankan ulang dengan beberapa nilai $U$ dan memplot $v_s / v_c$ akan memetakan crossover-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note these caveats on the numbers. Threshold-based detection is biased slightly low, so a charge velocity a few percent under the published value is expected. The spin envelope is wide because the connected correlator sits closer to the noise floor, which is why the median of the scan rather than a single fit is quoted.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan beberapa catatan tentang angka-angka ini. Deteksi berbasis ambang cenderung sedikit bias ke bawah, jadi kecepatan muatan yang beberapa persen di bawah nilai yang dipublikasikan itu wajar. Envelope spin lebar karena korelator terhubung lebih dekat ke noise floor, itulah sebabnya yang dikutip adalah median dari hasil scan, bukan satu fit saja.\n"

